@startuml submission-completion
title Submitting a single-shot operation and delivering its completion\n(design/reactor.md, design/pool.md, design/execution.md)

skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left

participant "coroutine\n(the waiter)" as U
participant "reactor\non worker A" as R
participant "pool\n(operation slot)" as P
participant "kernel" as K
participant "sched\non worker A" as SA
participant "sched\non worker B" as SB

note over R, P
  **This is the single-shot path.** A multishot operation names the
  socket's handle and never a coroutine; its completions append to a queue
  in the socket slot, and the waiter lives in that slot's own
  queue-waiter cell. A cancel operation names no waiter at all.
end note

== Arming, inside park step 2 ==

U -> R : submit(operation, buffer)
R -> P : take a slot
activate P
R -> P : write the waiter cell — a counted\nreference to the coroutine, the entry index,\nthe epoch
note over P
  One writer, one emptier, one thread:
  the worker that owns the ring the
  operation goes to.
end note
R -> R : write into the submission ring
alt the submission answers at once, and that ends the wait\n(OR, or AND with nothing left outstanding)
  R --> U : an inline result
  U -> U : retire every entry armed so far and continue.\nSteps 3 and 4 do not run
else it answers at once under AND, entries still outstanding
  R --> U : an inline result, retire nothing
  U -> U : park steps 3 and 4
else it does not answer at once
  U -> U : park steps 3 and 4
end
SA -> R : the turn flushes the batch
R -> K : submissions

== The kernel answers ==

K -> R : completion
R -> P : resolve the handle, read the slot
alt the waiter cell holds a reference
  R -> P : move the reference out of the cell\ninto the wake payload
  R -> SA : wake(coroutine, entry, epoch, result)
  SA -> SA : **step 0 — dispatch on the state word**
  group four outcomes
    alt the word names this worker
      SA -> U : steps 1..4 — the epoch test, the result\nstore, decidedness, retirement
      alt ordinary
        SA -> SA : step 5 — store Woken, enqueue\ninto this worker's private list
      else the move path — a declaring actor,\na loaded owner, no foreign frame,\nthe move unspent
        SA -> SA : store-release WokenShared, push to the\nshared ready set, ring a sleeper
      end
    else the word names worker B\n(a declaring actor only)
      SA -> SB : post the payload into B's intake queue
      SA -> SB : ring B through the worker driver's waker
      SB -> U : steps 1..5 run there
    else WokenShared\n(a declaring actor only)
      SA -> SA : drop a wake and a resolution;\nfor a cancel write the byte and\nre-read the word — the answer\nfollows the re-read
    else Terminal
      SA -> SA : drop the signal and release what it\ncarried; a cancel's promise is\nresolved *already finished*
    end
  end
else the cell is empty
  R -> P : read an empty cell
  note over P
    Two events empty it, both on this worker:
    the retire of the entry — phase 0 of the
    kernel cancel — and an earlier completion
    of this same operation, which already moved
    the reference into its own wake payload.
  end note
  R -> R : wake nobody
end

== Release ==

R -> P : decrement the owed count
alt the count is not zero
  R -> R : a zero-copy send still owes its\nnotification; a cancelled operation\nstill owes the cancel's completion.\nHold the slot and the buffer
else zero
  P -> P : store free, publish to the retire list
  deactivate P
end
note over P
  The slot becomes takeable only after every worker
  has passed a quiescent point. That is one of the
  four conditions under which a 32-bit generation is
  safe; the other three are in design/pool.md.
end note

@enduml
